{
  "uid": "qp-client",
  "title": "Client",
  "description": "What the browsers report through the ingest: page load time, client errors and warnings, what the ingest dropped, and where respondents abandoned. Client-reported and spoofable.",
  "tags": [
    "questionnaire-platform",
    "client"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": []
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Page loads",
      "description": "Respondent page loads that browsers reported as page.loaded. Client-reported and unauthenticated, so a product measure and never an access or billing input (O23).",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(browser_page_load_duration_milliseconds_count[$__range]))",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Page load p75",
      "description": "The 75th percentile of the time from navigation start to the end of the load event, over the selected range. The alert fires above 4000 ms for 30 minutes.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.75, sum by (le) (rate(browser_page_load_duration_milliseconds_bucket[$__range])))",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "decimals": 0,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 4000
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "id": 2,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 4,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Client errors",
      "description": "client.error log lines the ingest wrote over the selected range. It counts log lines, since the ingest keeps no counter per client event, so it depends on the log pipeline and on Loki's retention.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.error\" [$__range]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "queryType": "instant"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "id": 3,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Errors per page load",
      "description": "client.error lines over page.loaded lines. Errors from the admin app count in the numerator and only the respondent reports page loads, so read it as a trend. The alert fires above 5% over 30 minutes with at least 20 page loads.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.error\" [$__range])) or vector(0)) / sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"page.loaded\" [$__range]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "queryType": "instant"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "decimals": 2,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "id": 4,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Client warnings",
      "description": "client.warn lines: a query or mutation the admin did not handle, and a request that never connected from the respondent.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum(count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.warn\" [$__range]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "queryType": "instant"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "id": 5,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Browser fields dropped",
      "description": "Fields and events the ingest dropped over the selected range, by any reason. See Browser fields the ingest dropped for which.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(telemetry_ingest_dropped_total[$__range]))",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "id": 6,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Client events by level",
      "description": "Every event a browser sent that the ingest kept, by log level. The domain events session.abandoned and page.loaded log at info.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (detected_level) (count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} | telemetry_source=\"browser\" [$__interval]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{detected_level}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 7,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Page load duration percentiles",
      "description": "Median, p75 and p95 of the respondent's page load duration. It is the browser's own clock, so it includes the network the respondent is on.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.5, sum by (le) (rate(browser_page_load_duration_milliseconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "p50"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.75, sum by (le) (rate(browser_page_load_duration_milliseconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "p75"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(browser_page_load_duration_milliseconds_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 8,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Client warnings and errors",
      "description": "client.warn and client.error lines over time. A client line carries no message: its level is its name, and its meaning is its error type, frames and screen.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (detected_level) (count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.\" | detected_level=~\"warn|error\" [$__interval]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{detected_level}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 9,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Page loads",
      "description": "Respondent page loads per interval.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(increase(browser_page_load_duration_milliseconds_count[$__rate_interval]))",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 10,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 12,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Client errors by error type",
      "description": "The error's class name, never its message. An empty type is a rejection or a throw that was not an Error.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (error_type) (count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.error\" [$__interval]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{error_type}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 11,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 20,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Client errors by screen",
      "description": "The screen is a route template, /q/:questionnaireId for the respondent and the router's route id for the admin, never a URL.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (http_route) (count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.error\" [$__interval]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{http_route}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 12,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 20,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Browser fields the ingest dropped",
      "description": "The ingest keeps each event and strips a field outside the registry or an event's own list (O17). A build that sends a field the ingest does not list shows here as unknown_field.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum by (telemetry_ingest_reason) (increase(telemetry_ingest_dropped_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "legendFormat": "{{telemetry_ingest_reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      },
      "id": 13,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bargauge",
      "title": "Sessions abandoned, by last item",
      "description": "Where sessions were when the page was hidden: the last item the respondent changed, from the session.abandoned lines, over the selected range. It counts a session once however often the page was hidden, and a session that goes on to complete is still counted. The ten items with the most.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "topk(10, sum by (questionnaire_last_item_id) (count_over_time({service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"session.abandoned\" | telemetry_source=\"browser\" [$__range])))",
          "editorMode": "code",
          "queryType": "instant",
          "legendFormat": "{{questionnaire_last_item_id}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "displayMode": "gradient"
      },
      "id": 14,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "logs",
      "title": "Client warnings and errors, as logged",
      "description": "The ingest's log lines for browser warnings and errors: the error type, the frames and the screen, no message. Open a record's trace_id to reach the request that carried it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "loki",
        "uid": "loki"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "loki",
            "uid": "loki"
          },
          "expr": "{service_name=~\"qp-.+\"} |= \"client.\" | detected_level=~\"warn|error\"",
          "editorMode": "code"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending",
        "enableLogDetails": true
      },
      "id": 15,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "What this dashboard cannot show",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Beacon delivery.** `sent`, `beaconed` and the drop counts are kept by each tab's queue and never reach the server, so there is no series for them. A beacon the browser refused is a batch the ingest never saw.\n\n**Counts of client events.** The ingest logs each accepted client event and keeps no counter per event, so the error and warning panels count log lines and depend on the log pipeline. A counter by level would let them, and a share of dropped over received events, move to Prometheus.\n\n**Abandonment.** The counter for `session.abandoned` is on the Respondent funnel dashboard. A page hidden and shown again still counts once, and a session that completes afterwards has both events, so the ratio has no absolute threshold and no alert.\n\nEvery browser event is client-reported and unauthenticated: it feeds product understanding, not access or billing decisions (O23)."
      },
      "id": 16,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      }
    }
  ]
}
